<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Football War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1969">1969</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Hundred Hours' War, Soccer War</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Football War was a brief war between El <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/salvador">Salvador</a> and Honduras in July 1969, also called the Hundred Hours' War. Its causes were land disputes and the expulsion of Salvadoran migrants from Honduras, and it coincided with riots at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fifa-world-cup">World Cup</a> qualifying matches between the two countries. About 3,000 people died before the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/organization-of-american-states">Organization of American States</a> arranged a ceasefire, and a peace treaty followed only in 1980.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/football-war.jpg" alt="Football War" width="320" height="166" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: JuanJose1969 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Honduras_and_El_Salvador_map.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
